  "result": "I've written the plan for `click.KeyValue` but haven't changed any code yet, since we're still in planning mode. The usual tool for asking you to approve the plan isn't available here, so please read it at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-sleepy-book.md` and tell me whether to go ahead.\n\n**What the plan does:**\n1. **`src/click/types.py`:** adds a `KeyValue` class next to the existing UUID type, using the same error handling. It splits the input on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` becomes `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`. If there's no `=` or the key is empty, it fails with `'<value>' is not a valid key=value pair.` An empty value (`a=`) is allowed. Help text will show the option as `--set KEY=VALUE`.\n2. **`src/click/__init__.py`:** exports it as `click.KeyValue`.\n3. **`docs/api.md`:** adds an entry in the Types section.\n4. **`CHANGES.md`:** the latest section is 8.5.0, which is already released, so the entry goes in a new unreleased 8.6.0 section.\n5. **Tests in `tests/test_types.py`:**\n   - a normal pair\n   - a value that contains `=`\n   - an empty value\n   - `multiple=True` turned into a `dict`\n   - the two failure cases (`novalue` and `=value`) exit with an error and show the required message\n\n   I may also add an entry to `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nOnce it's built, I'll run `pytest` on those two test files and then the full suite.\n\n**Decision for you:** I'm planning to allow an empty value and not trim spaces around the key. Your spec doesn't cover either; say if you want them handled differently.",
